lineNoT -- a refusal's [line N] is the true file line of the top-level statement (Tony, 2026-11-18; seal 506's step A, SEQ 694).
The counter starts at 1, and the newlines a quoted string, a (...#) literal or a code={ } body swallows join it when the token
is taken. Rows in genLadder/pop.sh; each call is to a name defined nowhere, which refuses by name (undefined-call).
LN-1  lnOne on line 1 reads [line 1].
LN-2  lnTwo after a three-line quoted string reads [line 7].
LN-3  lnThree after a three-line (...#) literal and a four-line code body reads [line 17].
LN-4  lnFour two lines on reads [line 19].
